error[NK2308]: The lambda of `map` hands back a view of a line of the stream, which lives in a buffer of the stream's pool only for the call that sees it.
  --> tests/a_line_handed_on_by_map_is_refused.nika:8:5
   |
 8 |     let trimmed = io::lines().map(fn(l) { l.trim() }).count()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A stream reads into a fixed pool of buffers, and a step over it sees each line for one turn; what the step hands on is kept past that turn.
   = help: Hand back text of its own (`.clone()` of the line), or copy each line first with `.cloned()`.
1 view of a stream kept in a place that grows
